*.pem
*.key
keypairs/
target/
test-ledger/
.DS_Store

# Solana build output. The program keypair is a PRIVATE KEY — whoever holds it
# controls the program address and can deploy to it. It must never be committed;
# back it up out of band. The program's public address is in Anchor.toml and
# declare_id!(), which is all anyone needs to verify a deployment.
target/
**/*-keypair.json

# Next.js regenerates this on every dev/build, and its contents differ between
# the two — committing it means a permanently dirty tree. CI runs the build
# before the typecheck, so it always exists when tsconfig needs it.
next-env.d.ts
